{"id": "aa5c193dcbe9e385:tutorial:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:d32fd3251dbb5a91", "source_id": "aa5c193dcbe9e385", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-accounts/tax-advantaged-accounts/retirement-savings/403b-and-457b-plans", "topic": "403(b) and 457(b) Plans", "subtopic": "403(b) and 457(b) Plans", "content_type": "tutorial", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "These pre-tax contributions and their investment earnings will not be taxed until you withdraw the money, typically after you retire.", "question": null, "answer": "403(b) and 457(b) plans are tax-deferred retirement savings programs that certain employers may offer. You can contribute pre-tax money from your paycheck to invest in products offered through the plan. The contributions and their investment earnings generally are not taxed until you withdraw the money, typically after retirement. Some employers offer both types of plan and allow employees to contribute to both.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1134, "output_tokens": 262}}
{"id": "aa5c193dcbe9e385:qa:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:d32fd3251dbb5a91", "source_id": "aa5c193dcbe9e385", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-accounts/tax-advantaged-accounts/retirement-savings/403b-and-457b-plans", "topic": "403(b) and 457(b) Plans", "subtopic": "403(b) and 457(b) Plans", "content_type": "qa", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "These pre-tax contributions and their investment earnings will not be taxed until you withdraw the money, typically after you retire.", "question": "When are contributions and investment earnings in 403(b) and 457(b) plans generally taxed?", "answer": "They are generally taxed when you withdraw the money, typically after you retire.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1134, "output_tokens": 143}}
{"id": "aa5c193dcbe9e385:misconception:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:d32fd3251dbb5a91", "source_id": "aa5c193dcbe9e385", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-accounts/tax-advantaged-accounts/retirement-savings/403b-and-457b-plans", "topic": "403(b) and 457(b) Plans", "subtopic": "403(b) and 457(b) Plans", "content_type": "misconception", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "derived_from_source", "source_evidence": "Some employers offer both 403(b) and 457(b) plans and allow you to contribute to both plans.", "question": "Misconception: If I have a 403(b), I cannot also contribute to a 457(b).", "answer": "That is not always true. Some employers offer both plans and allow contributions to both. Check with your employer to find out whether both are available to you.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1134, "output_tokens": 195}}
{"id": "aa5c193dcbe9e385:tutorial:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:6e18e63b74ca4992", "source_id": "aa5c193dcbe9e385", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-accounts/tax-advantaged-accounts/retirement-savings/403b-and-457b-plans", "topic": "403(b) and 457(b) Plans", "subtopic": "403(b) vs. 457(b) Employer Eligibility", "content_type": "tutorial", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "Employers such as public educational institutions (public schools, colleges, and universities), certain non-profits, and churches or church-related organizations may offer 403(b) plans. Employers such as state and local government agencies and certain non-profit organizations may offer 457(b) plans.", "question": null, "answer": "Employer eligibility differs by plan type. Public educational institutions, certain nonprofits, and churches or church-related organizations may offer 403(b) plans. State and local government agencies and certain nonprofits may offer 457(b) plans. Some employers may offer both plans, so check with your employer to learn which are available.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1136, "output_tokens": 207}}
{"id": "aa5c193dcbe9e385:qa:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:6e18e63b74ca4992", "source_id": "aa5c193dcbe9e385", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-accounts/tax-advantaged-accounts/retirement-savings/403b-and-457b-plans", "topic": "403(b) and 457(b) Plans", "subtopic": "403(b) vs. 457(b) Employer Eligibility", "content_type": "qa", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "Employers such as public educational institutions (public schools, colleges, and universities), certain non-profits, and churches or church-related organizations may offer 403(b) plans.  Employers such as state and local government agencies and certain non-profit organizations may offer 457(b) plans.", "question": "What types of employers may offer 403(b) plans, and what types may offer 457(b) plans?", "answer": "Public educational institutions, certain nonprofits, and churches or church-related organizations may offer 403(b) plans. State and local government agencies and certain nonprofits may offer 457(b) plans. Some employers offer both, so check with your employer to learn what plans are available.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1136, "output_tokens": 222}}
{"id": "aa5c193dcbe9e385:misconception:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:6e18e63b74ca4992", "source_id": "aa5c193dcbe9e385", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-accounts/tax-advantaged-accounts/retirement-savings/403b-and-457b-plans", "topic": "403(b) and 457(b) Plans", "subtopic": "403(b) vs. 457(b) Employer Eligibility", "content_type": "misconception", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "derived_from_source", "source_evidence": "Employers such as state and local government agencies and certain non-profit organizations may offer 457(b) plans.", "question": "Misconception: Only state and local government employers can offer 457(b) plans.", "answer": "Correction: State and local government agencies may offer 457(b) plans, but they are not the only possible employers. Certain nonprofit organizations may offer them as well.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1136, "output_tokens": 193}}
{"id": "aa5c193dcbe9e385:tutorial:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:1cd1953e10a4f18d", "source_id": "aa5c193dcbe9e385", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-accounts/tax-advantaged-accounts/retirement-savings/403b-and-457b-plans", "topic": "403(b) and 457(b) Plans", "subtopic": "Pre-Tax Contributions and Tax-Deferred Growth", "content_type": "tutorial", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "These pre-tax contributions and their investment earnings will not be taxed until you withdraw the money, typically after you retire.", "question": null, "answer": "In a 403(b) or 457(b) plan, you can contribute pre-tax money from your paycheck to your account. The contributions and their investment earnings are generally not taxed until you withdraw the money, typically after retirement. This is tax-deferred growth: taxes are postponed until withdrawal, not eliminated.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1133, "output_tokens": 193}}
