{"id": "aa5c193dcbe9e385:misconception:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:1cd1953e10a4f18d", "source_id": "aa5c193dcbe9e385", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-accounts/tax-advantaged-accounts/retirement-savings/403b-and-457b-plans", "topic": "403(b) and 457(b) Plans", "subtopic": "Pre-Tax Contributions and Tax-Deferred Growth", "content_type": "misconception", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "derived_from_source", "source_evidence": "These pre-tax contributions and their investment earnings will not be taxed until you withdraw the money, typically after you retire.", "question": "Misconception: Money contributed to a 403(b) or 457(b), and any investment earnings, are never taxed.", "answer": "Correction: The source describes the tax treatment as deferred, not tax-free. Pre-tax contributions and their investment earnings are not taxed until the money is withdrawn, typically after retirement.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1133, "output_tokens": 196}}
{"id": "aa5c193dcbe9e385:tutorial:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:5ad6d1cdf84ffb12", "source_id": "aa5c193dcbe9e385", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-accounts/tax-advantaged-accounts/retirement-savings/403b-and-457b-plans", "topic": "403(b) and 457(b) Plans", "subtopic": "Mutual Funds and Annuities in Retirement Plans", "content_type": "tutorial", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "Typically, 403(b) and 457(b) plans offer two types of investment products – mutual funds and annuities.", "question": null, "answer": "403(b) and 457(b) plans typically offer mutual funds and annuities as investment options. A mutual fund share is a security regulated by the SEC. An annuity is a contract with an insurance company; depending on its type, it may be regulated by state insurance commissions, the SEC, or both.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1133, "output_tokens": 196}}
{"id": "aa5c193dcbe9e385:qa:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:5ad6d1cdf84ffb12", "source_id": "aa5c193dcbe9e385", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-accounts/tax-advantaged-accounts/retirement-savings/403b-and-457b-plans", "topic": "403(b) and 457(b) Plans", "subtopic": "Mutual Funds and Annuities in Retirement Plans", "content_type": "qa", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "Shares of a mutual fund are securities and are regulated by the SEC. An annuity is a contract between you and an insurance company.", "question": "In a 403(b) or 457(b) plan, how does a mutual fund differ from an annuity?", "answer": "A mutual fund is made up of shares that are securities regulated by the SEC. An annuity is a contract with an insurance company; depending on its type, it may be regulated by state insurance commissions, the SEC, or both.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1133, "output_tokens": 307}}
{"id": "aa5c193dcbe9e385:misconception:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:5ad6d1cdf84ffb12", "source_id": "aa5c193dcbe9e385", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-accounts/tax-advantaged-accounts/retirement-savings/403b-and-457b-plans", "topic": "403(b) and 457(b) Plans", "subtopic": "Mutual Funds and Annuities in Retirement Plans", "content_type": "misconception", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "derived_from_source", "source_evidence": "Shares of a mutual fund are securities and are regulated by the SEC. An annuity is a contract between you and an insurance company.", "question": "Misconception: Mutual funds and annuities are the same kind of investment product and are regulated in the same way.", "answer": "Correction: 403(b) and 457(b) plans may offer both mutual funds and annuities, but they are different products. Mutual fund shares are securities regulated by the SEC. An annuity is a contract with an insurance company; depending on its type, it may be regulated by state insurance commissions, the SEC, or both.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1133, "output_tokens": 240}}
